{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Manually diagnosing autocorrelation functions (ACF) and partial autocorrelation functions (PACF) to select ARIMA orders is time-consuming and error-prone. Standard automated packages like R’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forecast::auto.arima"},{"text":" or Python’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pmdarima"},{"text":" search across candidate orders sequentially.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AutoARIMA"},{"text":" evaluates the entire hyperparameter lattice simultaneously across all CPU cores on Apple Silicon using structured Swift Concurrency (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withThrowingTaskGroup"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Grid Search Architecture","anchor":"Grid-Search-Architecture","type":"heading"},{"code":["           Observed Time Series [y_1, y_2, ..., y_N]","                               │","       ┌───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┐","       ▼                       ▼                       ▼","ARIMA(1, 1, 0)          ARIMA(2, 1, 1)          ARIMA(0, 1, 2)","Task 1                  Task 2                  Task 3","   │                       │                       │","   ├─ Hannan-Rissanen      ├─ Hannan-Rissanen      ├─ Hannan-Rissanen","   └─ Compute AIC\/BIC      └─ Compute AIC\/BIC      └─ Compute AIC\/BIC","       │                       │                       │","       └───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┘","                               ▼","                withThrowingTaskGroup Collector","                               │","                               ▼","                 Sorted Leaderboard & Best Model"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"level":3,"text":"Information Criteria","anchor":"Information-Criteria","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"AIC (Akaike Information Criterion)","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Penalizes model complexity while rewarding likelihood:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"$$\\text{AIC} = 2k - 2\\ln(L)$$"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"BIC (Bayesian Information Criterion)","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Imposes a stronger penalty proportional to sample size:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"$$\\text{BIC} = k\\ln(N) - 2\\ln(L)$$"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"text":"Example Usage","anchor":"Example-Usage","type":"heading"},{"code":["import SwiftForecast","","\/\/ 1. Initialize AutoARIMA with bounded search ranges","let autoArima = AutoARIMA(","    maxP: 3,","    maxD: 2,","    maxQ: 3,","    criterion: .aic",")","","\/\/ 2. Concurrently fit candidates across all cores","let result = try await autoArima.fit(series: historicalPrices)","print(\"Optimal Order: \\(autoArima.bestOrder!) with AIC: \\(autoArima.bestScore!)\")","","\/\/ 3. Generate multi-step forecasts","let forecast = try await autoArima.forecast(horizon: 12)","print(\"Forecasted points: \\(forecast.forecast.predictions)\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Automated Time Series","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMA","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAOrder","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMACriterion"],"anchor":"Automated-Time-Series"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","modules":[{"name":"SwiftForecast"}],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Concurrent Order Selection with AutoARIMA"},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Discover optimal autoregressive, integrated, and moving average orders across ((p, d, q) \\times (P, D, Q)_s) grids using p